KG42.register("rules-4ab220da9027c5e784f89341",{"id":"41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R007","paper":"41-data_center_local_markets","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"The market operator determines the market clearing price for energy trading. Scope: Auction-based local energy market alternative described in the paper. Condition: The local energy market uses the auction-based alternative.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Auction-based local energy market alternative described in the paper.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The market operator determines the market clearing price for energy trading. Scope: Auction-based local energy market alternative described in the paper. Condition: The local energy market uses the auction-based alternative.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature / Introduction","anchor_text":"more practical scenario would be enabling IDCs to participate in local energy markets in power distr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Unlike grid-scale energy markets, the participants in a local energy market can have dual roles: in some time points, it can act as an energy buyer to purchase deficit energy from the market; in some other time points, it can act as an energy seller to sell the surplus energy to the market. Both auction market-based and Peer-to-Peer (P2P) negotiation-based mechanisms have been studied for the local energy trading. In the former, energy consumers and producers submit energy purchase/selling bids to an auction-based marketplace, and the market operator stacks the bids and determines the market clearing price for energy trading. In the latter, energy consumers and producers autonomously negotiate the price and amount of energy trading in a P2P manner [11]."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The only source support for R007 is the auction-mechanism background, which names an operator action and a clearing price but supplies no decision variable, design-selection variable, or domain assigned to this rule. The CSP proposed price pi_k^T(t) appearing in other rules is not declared here and is not the operator-determined clearing price.","empty_theta_reason":"No parameter is declared for R007. The passage mentions bids and a clearing price but does not give a symbol, numeric value, coefficient, unit, index, or domain that this frozen rule defines."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","quote":"the market operator stacks the bids and determines the market clearing price for energy trading."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"6c2441cb295bd640f0a86c7655bd33bc92035540fb9cf1cdbddb81d73913cc72","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule and its only supporting passage (v141-b-g01-E02) describe an auction-based local-energy-market background in prose: consumers and producers submit purchase/selling bids and 'the market operator stacks the bids and determines the market clearing price for energy trading.' The passage supplies no clearing-price expression, operator objective, bid-stacking function, variable or parameter definitions, units, domains, or solution rule for this operator-determined price. The paper's formal price equations (Eqs. 6-7 and 26-27) concern the CSP's proposed purchase/selling price and belong to the coordination.price_signal/pricing treatment outside this frozen R007 operator-to-pricing.local edge; they cannot be moved into R007 without changing the frozen graph. Thus C001 remains a source-grounded procedural statement, and applicability is non_mathematical rather than formalized. B evidence remains unreviewed under this experiment; no independent source audit is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is bound to the frozen operator-to-pricing edge E001. The quoted source states that the market operator stacks bids and determines the market clearing price; because this is prose background with no formal clearing expression, the binding records provenance only and does not assert a formula."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
